==Strategy==
Welcome to the "new" Otherworld Colosseum, where the rule is yet another beneficial one for you: any Ubers you send out get duplicated, giving them twice the damage and twice the health to tank through enemies. Doesn't this mean that the stages are going to be really easy? Nope. To compensate for this extremely strong rule, each and every one of these stages have ridiculous stage designs featuring unreal enemy spam that, as a result, makes these stages agonizingly painful with or without Ubers.

Even the first stage of this Colosseum isn't exempt to this, as this stage features two buffed Bun Buns, a Professor A. to snipe your Floating counters, a Tackey to kill your own sniper units, a random Capy, and Brollows as well as Shadow Boxer Ks to tear through your defense. The result is a ferocious stage that you can either try to rush down, or you can endure.

If you're trying to rush this stage, Double Bounty the Doge Dark, kill the Shadow Boxer K, and then use Talented [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to beat the base down. Use [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]] to clear out Brollow hordes as well.

===Recommended Ubers===
Due to this Colosseum's Rule, any Uber Rare Cats mentioned will be twice as effective.
*Anti-Floating Ubers: Examples include [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Daliasan]], [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Windy α]], [[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Hanzo]], [[The 6th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 6th Angel]], and [[Vampiric Yukimura]]. These units can help demolish Bun Bun early and let you win quicker, although be careful with snipers due to Tackey's presence.

